Jab ek hi cheez ke kai vikalp ho, to lambe if-else ki jagah **switch** saaf padta hai:

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    int din = 3;
    switch (din) {
        case 1: printf("Somvaar"); break;
        case 2: printf("Mangalvaar"); break;
        case 3: printf("Budhvaar"); break;
        case 4: printf("Guruvaar"); break;
        case 5: printf("Shukravaar"); break;
        case 6: printf("Shanivaar"); break;
        case 7: printf("Ravivaar"); break;
        default: printf("Galat number");
    }
    return 0;
}
```

Output: `Budhvaar`

- `break` na lagao to program agle case me bhi ghus jayega (fall through)
- Koi case na mile to `default` chalta hai
- switch sirf int aur char par chalta hai, float par nahi

Ternary operator if-else ka **ek line wala chhota roop** hai:

`shart ? sahi_ho_to_ye : warna_ye`

```c
#include <stdio.h>

