Recursion matlab — function **khud ko hi** bulaye. Har bulave par kaam thoda chhota hota jata hai, aur ek jagah rukna (base case) lazmi hai.

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int fact(int n) {
    if (n == 0)
        return 1;              // rukne ki jagah (base case)
    return n * fact(n - 1);    // khud ko chhote number se bulaya
}

int main() {
    printf("5 ka factorial = %d", fact(5));
    return 0;
}
```

Output: `5 ka factorial = 120`

Kaam aise hua: fact(5) = 5 x fact(4) = 5 x 4 x fact(3) ... = 5 x 4 x 3 x 2 x 1 = 120.

⚠️ Base case bhool gaye to function khud ko bulata rahega aur program crash (stack overflow) ho jayega.

isPrime function — 1 matlab prime, 0 matlab nahi:

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int isPrime(int n) {
    if (n < 2) return 0;
    for (int i = 2; i * i <= n; i++) {
        if (n % i == 0)
            return 0;          // bhajak mil gaya, prime nahi
    }
    return 1;
}

int main() {
    int n = 29;
    if (isPrime(n))
        printf("%d PRIME hai", n);
    else
        printf("%d PRIME nahi hai", n);
    return 0;
}
```

Output: `29 PRIME hai`

Function banane ka fayda dikho — ab main me kitne bhi number check karne ho, bas `isPrime(number)` bulana hai. Bhajak milte hi `return 0` se function wahi se wapas aa jata hai, pura loop chalane ki zaroorat nahi.

