Aam taur par dabbe (variable/array) pehle se tay aakar ke bante hain. **malloc** program chalte samay (runtime par) zaroorat ke hisaab se jagah mangta hai — dynamic memory.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    int *p = (int *)malloc(5 * sizeof(int));  // 5 int ki jagah mangi
    if (p == NULL) {
        printf("Jagah nahi mili");
        return 1;
    }
    for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++)
        p[i] = (i + 1) * 10;
    for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++)
        printf("%d ", p[i]);
    free(p);        // kaam khatm, jagah wapas - ye bhoolna galti hai
    return 0;
}
```

Output: `10 20 30 40 50`

- Fayda: user jitna data de, utni hi jagah — pehle se andaza nahi lagana
- `free()` se jagah wapas karna lazmi hai, warna program jagah khata rahega (memory leak)

