```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class CalcInput {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Pehla number: ");
        double a = sc.nextDouble();
        System.out.print("Operation (+ - * /): ");
        char op = sc.next().charAt(0);
        System.out.print("Dusra number: ");
        double b = sc.nextDouble();
        if (op == '+') System.out.println("Jawab = " + (a + b));
        else if (op == '-') System.out.println("Jawab = " + (a - b));
        else if (op == '*') System.out.println("Jawab = " + (a * b));
        else if (op == '/') System.out.println("Jawab = " + (a / b));
        else System.out.println("Galat operation");
    }
}
```

`sc.next().charAt(0)` se user ke likhe shabd ka pehla akshar (operation) mil jata hai. double liya hai taaki bhag me dashamlav bhi aaye.

