`'aeiou'.includes(ch)` — chhoti list me hona hi jaanch hai. Bade-chhote ki gadbad na ho isliye pehle `toLowerCase`.

Ek number, do button, ek screen:

```html
<h1 id="num">0</h1>
<button onclick="badlo(1)">+</button>
<button onclick="badlo(-1)">-</button>
<button onclick="badlo(0)">Reset</button>
<script>
let n = 0;
function badlo(k) {
  n = (k === 0) ? 0 : n + k;
  document.getElementById('num').textContent = n;
}
</script>
```

Ek hi function teen kaam — plus par 1, minus par -1, reset par seedha 0. Number `n` me rehta hai, screen bas use dikhati hai — ye 'data alag, dikhawa alag' wala soch har app me kaam aata hai.

Ek input, ek button, seedha formula:

```javascript
function nikalo() {
  let n = parseFloat(document.getElementById('n').value);
  if (isNaN(n)) { alert('Pehle number likho'); return; }
  document.getElementById('out').textContent = 'Jawab: ' + (n * 2);
}
```

`isNaN(n)` wala check khali ya galat input ko rokta hai — warna screen par NaN dikhega. Yahi dhacha (input → check → formula → jawab) har chhote tool me chalta hai.

Body par ek class, CSS me do rang:

```css
body { background: white; color: black; }
body.dark { background: #121212; color: #eee; }
```
```javascript
function darkBadlo() {
  document.body.classList.toggle('dark');
